A||N||14||Xtreme Fiero's||What clutch does every body use?||||5||
Z||000000||Xtreme Fiero's||10-26-2000||05:45 PM||||<BR>Well I will be picking up my 85 GT the first week in DEC. and I was wondering what would be the best clutch to use in it? The only high performance cluches I have ever used/ seen used all exploded (Centerforce DF) and a Three puck is not streteable. The car has a freshly rebuilt 2.8L and I will be putting in a used Isuzu (SP) 5-speed (&gt;65k) it will also have a basic NOS system (50-80hp) and basic bolt on stuf.<P>------------------<BR><P><BR>Tom D.<BR>85 GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> <BR>Black/Yellow 84 SE (4:10 4-speed)<P>Xtreme Kustumz<BR>http://community-2.webtv.net/XTREME_KUSTUMZ/XTREMEKUSTUMZ/||||reg||5
Z||000001||Ed||10-26-2000||06:15 PM||||This answer will probably be the expection, but here goes:<P>I replaced my original clutch in my '87 GT at 113,000 miles, only because it got oiled by a failed rear cam seal.  The clutch itself was in good condition for its age.  I drive the car "moderately hard" and don't drag race. <P>Many people have advised against the OEM "LUK" brand clutch, but my experience was satisfactory. So I had the dealer put in another LUK clutch, and I continue to be happy with it.  <P>Oh, oh, I reread your post.  You're going with nitrous.  I retract all my comments and wish you good "luk."<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||10-26-2000||06:21 PM||||The clutch that Fieroshop sells is of excellent quality. I have one.<BR>George I. Miller<BR>Fiero Shop, Richmond, Ca.<BR>(510) 23-FIERO<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||10-26-2000||06:23 PM||||88formula,<P>I am ordering George's clutch right after I get paid... tomorrow!<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||14
Z||000004||Xtreme Fiero's||10-26-2000||06:45 PM||||has anyone on the forum used the Fieroshop clutch yet? looks alot like a centerforce DF to me. How much is it?<P>I don't plan to drag race (Much  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) but I have been known to be prety hard on a car, Any car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> so I don't want to drop the cradle again just to change the clutch out after a high RPM 3-2 shift on a twisty back road and Ka-BOOM kevlar in my back (NOT A FUN THING)<P>two of my friends hav had thier CenterForce "Go out" MR-2 & 5.0 Mustang||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierosound||10-26-2000||07:44 PM||||Extreme...<P>"two of my friends hav had thier CenterForce "Go out" MR-2 & 5.0 Mustang"<P>What are you trying to say here??<P>||||reg||10
Z||000006||Xtreme Fiero's||10-26-2000||08:07 PM||||I think I want a high performance and Streetable clutch that won't wear out and will also add at least 50hp J/K  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> I am going to get the Fiero Shop Clutch I spoke with them today (20 min. ago) and they sound like they stand behind it. And thier word is goos enough for me.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Alex4mula||10-26-2000||09:42 PM||||Go with George's cluth at Fieroshop. I have it since last June with my 3.4 Formula and I recommend it. Grip is great and the feel is smooth. Great clutch.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||10-26-2000||10:21 PM||||I have the RAM HD clutch set in my stock Formula. It is fine for normal non-abusive work. But even with my tired 2.8 I can tell it wouldn't take much more than my engine puts out to have it start slipping. When the time comes to do the job again, I will be going with the clutch put out by the Fiero Shop.||||reg||1
Z||000009||fieroshop||10-27-2000||12:58 PM||||Thanks guys for recommending my clutch and also for wanting to purchase it.<BR>This clutch took over three months of research before we put it on a car for the first time. We researched all the clutches and found the problems associated with them and tried every trick and then some to eliminate them. It was also designed for better grip, better clamp load than all the clutches on the market. <BR>Our clamp load far exceeds everybody else's.<BR>Clamp loads on the other clutches is between 1200 and the highest of 1700. Ours is averaging 2200 lbs plus. <BR>Now you say that it would be harder on the pedal. And the answer is no. In fact, we find that our clutch is smoother, easier to push with your foot and also has much better grip then any clutch that we have seen out there.<BR>If you need more info, call me at the shop.<BR>The most important item that you must do is resurface your flywheel, if you don't there is no warranty whatsoever.<BR>Here is one more person who has my clutch and is wanting another.<P>Last year I bought one of your clutches for my 86 Fiero GT. It has performed flawlessly. I am very happy with this setup. It's installed behind a 3.4 V6.<BR>Easter Sunday the Fiero left the road 3/4 through a tight corner and made contact with a tree. The car cannot be repaired. I will salvage parts from this car as I prepare my next project. Fiero GT V8. I will not be using a V8 Archie kit. I would like a strong kelvar clutch from you. What are my options? Prices? Spec.?<P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif">   <P>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 10-27-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 10-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||StuGood||10-27-2000||01:01 PM||||I have used only one clutch in each of my Fieros, and have had no problems:  first pedal on the left  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000011||tgowens||10-27-2000||01:08 PM||||that's because the other pedal operates the "Winky Light" !!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                          <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT<BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group||||reg||1
