Z||000013||tgowens||10-28-2000||12:12 AM||||actually Stu, I got sidetracked when I came out to CA -- since I got to the Fiero Shop it has been non-stop -- I still have your address and will get a switch out to you to play with -- do you need the portion of the wiring harness too or just the switch??<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                          <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT<BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group||||reg||1
Z||000014||StuGood||10-29-2000||12:48 PM||||Either way.  Just the switch, if you want to save the wiring for somebody else's use   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  Otherwise, the made-to-order connector would make it easier for you to install.   <P>Since last time I wrote you, I modified the thing to make it a bit simpler + easier to install.  Just <B>like</B> an engineer, huh, can't leave well enough alone ?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Gonna try the new design out on the 1986 Gold SE, for functional test, and 'cause I want it on that car, too!     <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 10-29-2000).]||||reg||6
